{
 "group": "ultra-voxtral-clip-cli",
 "question": "Voxtral CLI decodes of the 935s clip: chunk length, overlap, KV precision, the weight-precision ladder at 60s / batch 16, fp16 at 30s / batch 32 / overlap 8, an instruction prompt, delay 480 against 2400ms, 8kHz round trip and 1.25x time-stretch, -14dB input with gain none and auto; and their rescore",
 "docs": [
  "docs/benchmarks/chunking.md",
  "docs/benchmarks/quantization.md",
  "docs/benchmarks/delay.md",
  "docs/benchmarks/input-level.md",
  "docs/benchmarks/prompt.md",
  "docs/benchmarks/reference/peak-memory.md",
  "RESULTS.md"
 ],
 "note": "In the commands $PY is the repo venv python, $CLIP the 935s clip (bench_out/corpus_timed/632a295d981d.wav), $REF its reference subtitles (the .srt beside it) and $D the queue directory bench_out/q7_20261015; hypotheses are not saved. The clip variants are corpus.json derived inputs clipattn14, clip8k and clipstretch125. CER (plain, kana, lenient) of every decode is the score_clip run (rescore_all.py over the written SRTs); the stats carry encode_s, decode_s, steps and peak memory.",
